IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cccfa-types`
IMPORT `cccfa-dates`

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — GOAL 3: HARDSHIP.
--
--   "May the debtor make this hardship application, and by when must the
--    creditor acknowledge it, ask for information and decide?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_52.txt — ss 55, 57, 57A.

§ `Goal 3 — hardship`

-- s 55 "(3) A debtor who makes an application under this section is not
-- entitled to make another application in relation to the same consumer
-- credit contract unless— (a) the application is made not less than 4 months
-- after the previous application is made; or (b) in the case of an
-- application that is made less than 4 months after ...,— (i) the creditor
-- agrees to consider the application; or (ii) the reasons ... are materially
-- different". s 57 "(1) A debtor may not make an application under section 55
-- if— (a) the debtor is in default ... and ... (i) has been in default for 2
-- weeks or more after receiving a repossession warning notice ...; or (ii)
-- has failed to make 4 or more consecutive periodic payments ...; or (iii) has
-- been in default for 2 months or more; or (b) it was reasonably foreseeable
-- ... (2) However, subsection (1)(a) does not prevent an application being
-- made after the debtor has remedied the default". "Not less than 4 months
-- after" the previous application: the 4 months run from the next day
-- (Legislation Act 2019 ss 54, 56), so the new application must come after
-- they end (fork F6; changed after the independent pass).
@ref ss 55(3), 57
@export Whether a debtor may make a hardship application under ss 55 and 57 of the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ): a further application only 4 months after the last, unless the creditor agrees or the reasons are materially different; and not while in default for 2 weeks after a repossession warning notice, after 4 consecutive missed payments, or for 2 months (unless remedied), nor if the inability was reasonably foreseeable when contracting. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN a IS A `Hardship application`  @desc The application date, any previous application, the creditor's agreement, the reasons, the default history, and foreseeability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hardship application may be made` a IF
        (CONSIDER a's `previous application made on`
         WHEN JUST previous THEN
                made GREATER THAN `the last day of a period of` 4 `months beginning with` (`the day` 1 `days after` previous)
             OR a's `the creditor agrees to consider it`
             OR a's `reasons materially different from before`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)
    AND (   a's `the default has been remedied`
         OR NOT (   a's `days in default after a repossession warning notice` AT LEAST 14
                 OR a's `consecutive periodic payments missed` AT LEAST 4
                 OR (CONSIDER a's `in default since`
                     WHEN JUST since THEN made AT LEAST `add months` since 2
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)))
    AND NOT a's `inability reasonably foreseeable when contracting`
    WHERE
        made MEANS a's `hardship application made on`

-- s 57A "(1) ... the creditor must ...: (a) within 5 working days after
-- receiving the application, acknowledge receipt ...: (b) within 10 working
-- days after receiving the application, request any further information ...:
-- (c) within 20 working days after receiving the application, ... decide ...
-- and give written notice ... (2) However, if the creditor has requested
-- further information ..., the time ... is the later of— (a) 10 working days
-- after receiving the further information; and (b) 20 working days after
-- making the request". Only a request made "in accordance with subsection
-- (1)(b)" — within its 10 working days — extends the time (added after the
-- independent pass).
@ref s 57A(1)-(2)
GIVEN received IS A DATE, matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to acknowledge a hardship application received on` received `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the` 5 `th working day after` received `, Matariki days` matariki

@ref s 57A(1)(b)
GIVEN received IS A DATE, matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request information on a hardship application received on` received `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the` 10 `th working day after` received `, Matariki days` matariki

@ref s 57A(1)(c), (2)
@export The last day for a creditor to decide a hardship application and notify the debtor under s 57A of the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ): 20 working days after receiving it; if further information was requested, the later of 10 working days after receiving the information and 20 working days after the request. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN received IS A DATE  @desc The day the application was received
      requested IS A MAYBE DATE  @desc The day further information was requested, if it was
      supplied IS A MAYBE DATE  @desc The day the further information was received, if it was
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to decide a hardship application received on` received `, information requested` requested `, supplied` supplied `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    CONSIDER requested
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the` 20 `th working day after` received `, Matariki days` matariki
    WHEN JUST asked THEN
        CONSIDER supplied
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 57A(2) needs the date the information was received`
        WHEN JUST got THEN
            IF   asked GREATER THAN `the` 10 `th working day after` received `, Matariki days` matariki
            THEN `the` 20 `th working day after` received `, Matariki days` matariki
            ELSE later (`the` 10 `th working day after` got `, Matariki days` matariki) (`the` 20 `th working day after` asked `, Matariki days` matariki)
    WHERE
        GIVEN x IS A DATE, y IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        later x y MEANS IF x GREATER THAN y THEN x ELSE y

`s 57A(2) needs the date the information was received` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 57A(2): the time runs from receipt of the further information, which has not been received"
